    stem: "An alloy is an intimate mixture of elements, usually metals. When 76.20 g of an alloy composed only of silver and copper were added to an excess of concentrated nitric acid the following reactions took place. Brown fumes of nitrogen(IV) oxide gas were released and 22.50 g of copper(II) nitrate were formed.\nAg (s) + 2HNO3 (aq) → AgNO3 (aq) + NO2 (g) + H2O (l)\nCu (s) + 4HNO3 (aq) → Cu(NO3)2 (aq) + 2NO2 (g) + 2H2O (l)",
