    stem: "The elements radium (Ra) and polonium (Po) were discovered on the basis of their radioactivity through the work of Marie and Pierre Curie. In 1902 they obtained 0.1 g of pure RaCl₂ from a tonne of pitchblende, the material remaining after uranium is extracted from its ore. In 1910 Marie Curie isolated pure radium. However she never succeeded in isolating pure polonium, in part because of its short half‐life. The nuclear equation below represents the alpha decay of polonium–210.",
