    stem: "Effervescent tablets typically contain a dry mixture of citric acid (C₆H₈O₇), tartaric acid (C₄H₆O₆) and sodium hydrogencarbonate (NaHCO₃). This mixture reacts when the tablet is placed in water, producing carbon dioxide gas, according to the following balanced chemical equations: C₆H₈O₇ + 3NaHCO₃ → Na₃C₆H₅O₇ + 3H₂O + 3CO₂ C₄H₆O₆ + 2NaHCO₃ → Na₂C₄H₄O₆ + 2H₂O + 2CO₂ An effervescent tablet contains 0.096 g of citric acid and 0.15 g of tartaric acid.",
