          "alt": "The marking scheme's own print of its answer to 2022 HL Q1(e)(iii), as the State Examinations Commission set it: the answer, 0.00368 (3.68 × 10⁻³, 23/6250) – 0.0037 moles of M²⁺ removed from one litre (3), then two routes: 0.000092 × 40 = 0.00368 ... moles (3), with [Multiply (ii) by 40 essential.]; or 25.0 × M over 1 = 9.2 × 0.010 over 1, so M = 0.00368 ... moles of M²⁺ removed from one litre (3).",
          "attribution": "SEC Leaving Certificate Chemistry 2022 Higher Level — © State Examinations Commission",
